# File: scripts/__tests__/validation-tiers.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-heavy-pool.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-steering-runtime.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/580-run-flagged-steering-validations-concurrently-in-the-verification-gate/requirements.md
Feature: Run flagged steering validations concurrently in the verification gate

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Flagged validations run at the same time
    Given a steering manifest with two applicable Phase 2 validations that both declare concurrent true
    When the verification gate runs
    Then both providers start before either one finishes
    And the gate's elapsed time is close to the longer of the two rather than their sum

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Unflagged validations keep today's serial behavior
    Given a manifest where some applicable Phase 2 validations omit concurrent or set it to false
    When the verification gate runs
    Then each unflagged validation runs while no other validation is running
    And a manifest with no concurrent keys produces the same execution order and artifact as before

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A failure does not stop the other concurrent validations
    Given two concurrent validations where one provider fails quickly and the other is still running
    When the gate runs
    Then the still-running validation completes and records its own result
    And the artifact contains a result for every applicable validation and the ceiling reflects the failure

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Results stay in manifest order
    Given concurrent validations that finish in a different order from the manifest
    When the verification artifact is written
    Then its results array lists validations in manifest order with the same fields as a serial run

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Heavy validations still take a pool slot
    Given a validation with heavy true and concurrent true and a heavy-job pool whose only slot is held
    When the gate runs
    Then that validation waits for a slot before its provider starts and records heavy slot and waitedMs
    And other concurrent validations that are not heavy start without waiting

  @SCN006
  Scenario: The Phase 1 deferral rule is unchanged
    Given a required local builtin.command validation that fails in Phase 1
    When Phase 2 runs concurrent project-provider validations
    Then those validations are recorded as incomplete with "deferred until required local validations pass"

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Cancelling the gate stops every running validation
    Given several concurrent validations in progress
    When the gate's abort signal fires
    Then every running provider is cancelled and every held heavy slot is released
    And each unfinished validation is recorded as non-passing

  @SCN008
  Scenario: An invalid flag is rejected
    Given a manifest validation whose concurrent value is not a boolean
    When the steering runtime loads the manifest
    Then loading fails with steering_validation_invalid naming concurrent
